      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Giant cysts of the liver are uncommon. Symptoms are related primarily to the mass effect of the enlarging cyst."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To highlight the challenges of management of giant simple hepatic cyst in a resource limited setting."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE REPORT",
          "content": "Presented is a 58-year-old seamstress with a 5-year history of an enlarging abdominal mass with easy satiety. Surgery revealed an exophytic giant simple hepatic cyst arising from liver segment IV that drained 4.6 litres of serous fluid."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Simple hepatic cyst can attain giant dimensions and should be considered in the differential diagnosis of intraabdominal masses."
        }
      ]},
